        "title": "test(semver-compare): unit tests for semver parsing, normalization, and comparison",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`src/infra/semver-compare.ts` exports 4 functions used by plugin install/update, ClawHub version ordering, and config version checks. It has zero dedicated test coverage — no `semver-compare.test.ts` exists.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe module handles non-trivial semver edge cases: legacy dot-beta normalization, prerelease identifier comparison (numeric-before-string semver precedence), build metadata stripping, and v-prefix tolerance. Without dedicated tests, regressions in these paths could silently break plugin update ordering or version compatibility checks.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **`src/infra/semver-compare.test.ts`** (new, 178 lines) — 27 test cases covering all 4 exports\n\n## Evidence\n\n```text\n$ npx vitest run src/infra/semver-compare.test.ts\n\n ✓ src/infra/semver-compare.test.ts (27 tests) 5ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  27 passed (27)\n```\n\n### Coverage breakdown\n\n| Function | Tests | Assertions |\n|----------|:-----:|:----------:|\n| `normalizeLegacyDotBetaVersion` | 6 | 6 |\n| `parseComparableSemver` | 9 | 11 |\n| `comparePrereleaseIdentifiers` | 6 | 12 |\n| `compareComparableSemver` | 6 | 7 |\n| **Total** | **27** | **36** |\n\n## Related\n\nN/A (self-contained test addition)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
